kind: research_run
id: research-run:decision-sufficiency:v0.1:first
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: Codex
recorded_date: 2026-09-30
experiment_status: experimental
source_ref: fixtures/decision-sufficiency.v0.1.json
purpose: >
  Determine whether a projection can erase a distinction required by an existing
  bounded execution gate, exhibit that loss, and recover an exact gate outcome.
finite_fixture_result:
  enumerated_states: 256
  gate_executable_states: 2
  gate_blocked_states: 254
  coarse_fibers: 1
  ambiguous_coarse_fibers: 1
  coarse_result: needs_refinement
  minimum_refinement_cardinality: 7
  all_minimum_refinement_count: 1
  excluded_candidate_fields: [display_label]
  refined_fibers: 128
  ambiguous_refined_fibers: 0
  interpretation: >
    The intentionally lossy approval summary cannot determine this exact modeled
    merge outcome. Seven independent gate conditions suffice and are necessary
    within the declared attribute set. The display label contributes nothing to
    recovering this decision. The counts are synthetic and are not event rates.
independent_verification:
  boolean_decision_rules: 256
  projections_per_rule: 8
  total_analyses: 2048
  method: >
    An independent pairwise oracle verifies every partition, outcome, ambiguity
    witness, minimum-cardinality subset, tie, and field-necessity witness over all
    Boolean decisions on three binary fields at every resolution.
breakdown_found:
  trigger: independent review of current applicability bindings
  mismatch: >
    Pinning the gate source alone omitted the adapter and baseline policy that
    also determine its answer. A changed baseline policy head could change every
    executable outcome while the four originally proposed bindings stayed equal.
  responsible_component: scripts/generate-decision-sufficiency-v0.1.mjs
  repair: >
    The evaluator binding now hashes gate source, adapter source, and baseline
    fixture together. A regression changes a valid policy head and confirms that
    the old receipt becomes stale without changing its historical content.
boundaries:
  fixture_is_synthetic: true
  live_effects: false
  grants_authority: false
  human_trials_run: 0
  population_efficacy_established: false
  gate_limit: >
    The reused gate checks that approvalBasis is present; it does not establish
    rightful approval or revocation status. Exact recovery is relative to this
    evaluator and finite domain, not a proof of complete authorization safety.
next_question: >
  Can Dave use the witness and refined View to identify the consequential
  distinction and reach the fixture-correct answer without extra explanation?
next_test:
  kind: single_participant_instrument_shakedown
  proposed_trials: 16
  status: not_run
  observations: [answer_correctness, missing_distinction_identified, time_to_answer, confusing_labels]
  limitation: >
    This shakedown can find interface problems. It cannot establish general human
    benefit, safety, calibration, or a population-level effect.
proof:
  covers: [finite_fixture_result, independent_verification, breakdown_found]
  generator: scripts/generate-decision-sufficiency-v0.1.mjs
  tests: tests/decision-sufficiency-v0.1.test.mjs
  output: fixtures/decision-sufficiency.v0.1.json
